      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After looking into how to implement udon worlds, I can’t figure out what even will allow me to get into controlling a avatar’s hand that current is holding a pick up and the user wants to slash or rotate their wrist.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-01-30T12:12:11.145Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In some vrchat worlds, a user can pick a melee weapon, but for a pc player using a melee weapon is kind of disorientating. Normally you move your mouse around (basically your head camera) to perform a slash. It would be nice for udon to have some actions options when something is held in hand to perform a default slash with the hand. \nFor example we pick up a sword with the left click of a mouse, when we click left click again and again and the game recognizes we are holding an object there is a udon option to say perform a slash such as a diagonal/horizontal/throw etc. That way you don’t have to move your mouse around (which is a really just controlling your head camera while your avatar just holds a sword in front of them). So ideally this could also work for things like bowling or something.",
